63. Transaction
BEGIN;

UPDATE employees
SET salary = salary + 5000
WHERE id = 1;

UPDATE employees
SET salary = salary + 5000
WHERE id = 2;

COMMIT;
64. ROLLBACK
BEGIN;

UPDATE employees
SET salary = 100000
WHERE id = 1;

ROLLBACK;

The update is undone.

65. SAVEPOINT
BEGIN;

UPDATE employees
SET salary = 100000
WHERE id = 1;

SAVEPOINT salary_update;

DELETE FROM employees
WHERE id = 2;

ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT salary_update;

COMMIT;

The salary update remains, while the delete is rolled back.

66. PostgreSQL Function

Now the important part you specifically asked for.

Create a custom function that calculates annual salary.

CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION hrms.calculate_annual_salary(
    monthly_salary NUMERIC
)
RETURNS NUMERIC
LANGUAGE plpgsql
AS $$
BEGIN
    RETURN monthly_salary * 12;
END;
$$;
