100. Identity Column – Modern PostgreSQL

Instead of SERIAL, modern PostgreSQL can use:

CREATE TABLE employees (
    id BIGINT GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100)
);

Or:

id BIGINT GENERATED BY DEFAULT AS IDENTITY

For new projects, identity columns are generally preferable to SERIAL.

