One particularly important concept

For PostgreSQL, remember this distinction:

-- Function: returns a value and can be used inside SQL
SELECT hrms.annual_salary(salary)
FROM hrms.employees;

versus:

-- Procedure: execute an operation
CALL hrms.increase_salary(10, 5000);

And for a real Laravel application, a common permission structure would be:

PostgreSQL
   │
   ├── Database: hrms
   │
   ├── Schema: hrms
   │
   ├── Roles
   │     ├── hrms_readonly
   │     ├── hrms_editor
   │     └── hrms_admin
   │
   ├── Tables
   │     ├── employees
   │     ├── departments
   │     └── employee_audit
   │
   ├── Views
   ├── Materialized Views
   ├── Functions
   ├── Procedures
   ├── Triggers
   └── Indexes

This is a good structure to understand for mid-to-large enterprise PostgreSQL applications.
